{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SoV9JiGuPxW1ruiERqjQhm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0161DNm56V7qYWDty1kimcr1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> scripts/ralph/progress.txt <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-058\n- Bug: post-blur ✓/✗ feedback in `CodeClozeWidget` rendered icons inline (correct) BUT showed the slot.hint inside a `display: 'block'` `<span>` BELOW the input, instead of as an end-of-line comment matching the lesson's source language. Fixed by replacing the block hint span with line-level inline comment spans rendered at the end of each `<pre>` line that contains an incorrect slot.\n- Extracted four pure helpers to `src/widgets/CodeCloze/feedbackComment.ts`: `commentPrefix(language)` → `'#'` for python (default) / `'//'` for js/ts; `findExistingCommentStart(line, prefix)` → string-aware search that ignores `#` / `//` inside `'..'` or `\"..\"` literals; `formatFeedbackComment(hints, prefix, hasExisting)` → returns `\"  # hint1; hint2\"` (no existing comment) or `\"; hint1; hint2\"` (append to existing comment, no new prefix); `groupSegmentsIntoLines(segments)` → splits the existing `parseTemplate` output on newlines so each rendered `<pre>` line owns its own slots + feedback span. Added `lineHasExistingComment(lineSegments, prefix)` thin wrapper that re-stringifies a line (slots stand in as `__SLOT__`) and runs `findExistingCommentStart`.\n- Added `src/widgets/CodeCloze/feedbackComment.test.ts` — 23 tests across the five helpers. Bug-repro tests: `formatFeedbackComment(['Use sum'], '#', false)` must return `\"  # Use sum\"` (would fail against the old block-style hint behaviour, which never produced a comment string at all); `formatFeedbackComment(['Use sum'], '#', true)` must return `\"; Use sum\"` (covers AC: \"When the line already has a comment, the feedback comment is appended after it without breaking syntax highlighting\"). Also covers js `//` prefix, string-aware comment detection, multi-hint join with `; `, empty/whitespace filter, slot-line grouping, mid-line slots.\n- Schema: added optional `language: 'python' | 'javascript' | 'typescript'` to `CodeClozeDataSchema` (defaults to python at the helper level — existing courses without `language` keep `#` prefix). Re-ran `npm run build:schemas` to regenerate `src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json` + `lesson.json`.\n- `CodeClozeWidget.tsx` changes: (a) replaced the `<pre>` segment-flat render with a `lines.map((lineSegs, lineIdx) => …)` render — each line is a `<span data-cloze-line data-line-index>` containing the line's text/slot segments followed by an optional `<span data-testid=\"cloze-line-feedback-<lineIdx>\" data-cloze-feedback>` with the formatted comment (italic, `var(--code-comment)` color); (b) `'\\n'` is emitted between lines (preserved by `<pre>` whiteSpace); (c) `SlotInput` lost its `showHint` prop and the `slotHintStyle` block-display span is gone; (d) icons gained `data-testid=\"cloze-slot-icon-<id>\"` + `data-icon=\"correct|incorrect\"` for testing; (e) wrapper span around input+icon got `whiteSpace: 'nowrap'`, and `slotIconStyle` got `display: 'inline-block'` — without both, the SVG icon was wrapping below the input inside the inline-block wrapper because lucide SVGs default to `display: block` and the inherited `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'` from `<pre>` allowed a break after the input.\n- Files changed: src/widgets/CodeCloze/CodeClozeWidget.tsx (modified — line-based render, removed block hint, added inline-block to icon, added nowrap to wrapper); src/widgets/CodeCloze/schema.ts (modified — `language` field added); src/widgets/CodeCloze/feedbackComment.ts (new); src/widgets/CodeCloze/feedbackComment.test.ts (new); src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json + lesson.json (regenerated).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 248/248 (was 225 → +23 new). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-058.js`, 15 assertions) passes against `/courses/cloze-test/lessons/box-blur` (template `def box_blur(values):\\n    total = {{aggregator}}(values)\\n    return total / {{divisor}}\\n`): types `avg` into aggregator → `data-slot-state=incorrect`, ✗ icon at correct boundingBox (right of input, vertically centered, gap < 30px), feedback span text starts with `\"  # \"` and contains the slot's hint, feedback boundingBox center y matches input center y (same row, not below); types `sum` → ✓ icon inline + feedback span removed; both slots wrong → exactly 2 feedback spans, one per line, both with `# ` prefix; no console errors. Screenshots at /tmp/US-058-correct.png and /tmp/US-058-both-wrong.png.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **`lucide-react` icons render as `<svg>` with `display: block` by default.** Inside an `inline-block` parent that inherits `whiteSpace: pre-wrap` (e.g. anything inside `<pre style=\"whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'\">`), the SVG forces a line break after the preceding inline element. Symptom: icon renders BELOW the input even though DOM order says \"after\". Fix needs BOTH `whiteSpace: 'nowrap'` on the wrapper AND `display: 'inline-block'` (or `'inline'`) on the icon style. Either alone is insufficient — nowrap doesn't override block-level child display, and inline-block on the icon still wraps if the wrapper allows breaks.\n  - **String-aware comment detection.** Naive `line.indexOf('#')` would falsely match `print(\"# not a comment\")`. The walking parser (track `inStr` quote char, advance past `\\\\`-escapes, only test the prefix when not inside a string) is short enough — ~20 lines — that it's not worth pulling in a tokenizer dep. Same pattern works for `//` against single-/double-quoted JS strings; we tested both. Doesn't handle Python triple-quotes or template literals — fine for cloze line scope (cloze templates are line-by-line by definition).\n  - **Line-based rendering inside `<pre>` with `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`.** To inject a per-line trailing element while preserving newline-driven line breaks, render each line as a wrapper `<span>` containing the line's content + optional trailing element, then emit a literal `'\\n'` text node between lines (skip the last). The `<pre>` parent renders the `\\n` as a real line break. This sidesteps the React fragment-newline quirk where `<>{line}{'\\n'}</>` works but `[line, '\\n']` arrays sometimes don't preserve the newline properly across React reconciliation.\n  - **Optional schema field rollout.** Adding `language: z.enum([...]).optional()` to a Zod data schema is a no-op for existing fixtures: `CodeClozeDataSchema.parse(rawData)` accepts records without the field, `validateSlotValue` is unaffected, and the helper defaults to `'python'` so `commentPrefix(undefined) → '#'`. No course migration needed. Don't forget to re-run `npm run build:schemas` so `src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json` reflects the new optional property — the json-schema is the contract for the LLM-side course-spec generation skill.\n  - **Bug-fix story TDD pattern (revisited from US-057).** The cleanest \"failing-test-before-fix\" expression for a UI bug is: extract the broken decision into pure helpers and write tests for the FIXED behavior. Here `formatFeedbackComment` returning `\"  # hint\"` is the fixed contract; against the old widget code (which rendered a block span and never produced a comment string at all), that test would fail because the helper didn't exist yet. AC satisfied without spinning up jsdom + react-testing-library.\n  - **`display: 'block'` on a hint span is the actual bug.** The README-level lesson here: when a parent renders an inline element trailing some other inline content, NEVER set the trailing element's display to `block` thinking \"it'll just stack below\" — yes it stacks, but it also disrupts inline-block parent sizing. If you want a line-break before the element, prefer a literal `'\\n'` text node between siblings (under a `<pre>` ancestor) or a flex column container — but in this case, the entire premise was wrong: the hint should NOT be on a separate line, it should be an inline comment.\n  - **Existing icons in `CodeClozeWidget` lacked test ids.** Added `data-testid=\"cloze-slot-icon-<id>\"` + `data-icon=\"correct|incorrect\"` for browser-test access. Generally: ANY decorative icon that has different states based on user input deserves a `data-testid` + `data-state` (or `data-icon`) attribute pair, even if no test currently uses it — bug-fix stories (this one) will need it within the lifetime of the codebase.\n---\nEOF\necho \"appended\"","description":"Append progress.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":277,"cache_read_input_tokens":136494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":277},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae8df7de-da98-42e4-9412-547c888ddf87","uuid":"304c10d1-3107-4788-a91a-728d6e2db3ec"}
